     {
      "start": 1940,
      "end": 1969,
      "headway_min": 720,
      "note": "The City of Miami, a seven-car coach streamliner, was inaugurated on 18 December 1940 and ran the 1,493 miles from Chicago to Miami, with the Illinois Central handling it as far as Birmingham and the Central of Georgia, Atlantic Coast Line and Florida East Coast carrying it on. It shared the district with the Seminole, which from 1950 left Chicago at 4 pm and reached Birmingham at 8.30 am and Jacksonville at 9 pm. headway_min is an estimate, not read off a timetable.",
      "sources": [
